-- title:
--   Points in both component closures are crossing points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage` for $p$, that is, a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular curve over $\mathbb Z$, including in particular a curve model `ratModel κ` over each algebraically closed field $κ$ of characteristic $p$ together with two closed immersions `compInf κ` and `compZero κ` of its underlying scheme into the base change of `DRModel p`. Let $O$ be a local commutative ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $κ$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $toκ \colon O \to κ$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $b =$ `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` for the induced morphism from the $κ$-base change of `DRModel p` to its $O$-base change, that is, the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathbb Z \to O$. The assertion is: for every point $x$ of the topological space of that $O$-base change which lies both in the closure of the image of the continuous map underlying `compInf κ` followed by $b$ and in the closure of the image of the continuous map underlying `compZero κ` followed by $b$, there exists a point $n$ of the scheme-theoretic intersection $\operatorname{pullback}(\mathtt{compInf } κ, \mathtt{compZero } κ)$ such that $x$ is the image of $n$ under the map on points induced by the first projection of that pullback followed by `compInf κ` followed by $b$. In other words, such an $x$ is the image of one of the crossing points of the two components.
--
--   Over $\mathbb F_p$ the special fibre of $X_0(p)$ is a union of two rational curves meeting exactly at the supersingular points (Deligne–Rapoport); the present statement is the point-set shadow of that picture for an arbitrary local base $O$ with maximal ideal $(p)$: a point lying in both component closures must come from the crossing scheme, here realised as the fibre product of the two component immersions. It is the unconditional form of a conditional statement that assumes the two generic points of the components have distinct images. It is used in the verification of the clauses `comp_prod`, `edgePt_exhaust` and `edgePt_transversal` of the resolved-model data, where the intersection points of the components of the special fibre must be identified with the crossing points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_exists_eq_baseChangeMap_crossing_of_mem_closure_of_mem_closure.lean

